stateDiagram-v2
    %% CURRENT implementation; sources and guards in transition inventory.
    state "ACTIVE id=1" as ACTIVE
    state "CONSUMED id=2" as CONSUMED
    state "REVOKED id=3" as REVOKED
    state "EXPIRED id=4 (declared; setter UNKNOWN)" as EXPIRED
    [*] --> ACTIVE
    ACTIVE --> CONSUMED: consume!
    ACTIVE --> REVOKED: revoke!
    CONSUMED --> CONSUMED: consume!
    CONSUMED --> REVOKED: revoke!
    REVOKED --> CONSUMED: consume!
    REVOKED --> REVOKED: revoke!
    EXPIRED --> CONSUMED: consume!
    EXPIRED --> REVOKED: revoke!
    note right of ACTIVE
        consume!/revoke! lack source/expiry guards.
        TTL is a predicate; EXPIRED setter UNKNOWN.
        Authentication proof does not issue a normal session.
    end note
